# The Layered Letter
Category: Miscellaneous  |  Points: 400 
Misc | Hard | 400 pts
Description:
A secret agent encoded a message in three layers inside a normal-looking text. Peel each layer using a different technique. The final flag uses leet speak — where some letters are replaced with numbers.

No programming needed. Every step can be done with free online tools or just your brain.

Flag format: flag{...}  

The Message:
[Paragraph 1]
Snakes often curl under rocks, especially during storms.
Every creature in nature adapts to survive long winters.
Calm oceans reveal endless beauty; turtles emerge safely.
Rare animals thrive only under natural conditions.
Every wild species holds incredible, natural, generous energy.

[Paragraph 2]
Silence often carries real exact truths.
Hidden answers reveal only what silent eyes see.
Find lies inside no gathered space.
Think hard every secret; zero options remain empty.

[Paragraph 3]
Czggp czn ocz nzbmzo rwz, nzxmzo rvt, ndbiy jaa, bzoozm lpdxfgt.

What to do:
1. Read the first letter of each sentence in paragraph 1 — top to bottom. You'll get a word.
2. In paragraph 2, read the last letter of each sentence — top to bottom. You'll get a number.
3. Use that number to Caesar-decode paragraph 3. Then apply leet rules to get the flag.
